    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0375" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/523</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to
                        the British Embassy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The British Embassy is informed that the Government of the United States has been
                    approached recently by several other governments with a request for an exchange
                    of views on the subject of postwar aviation, with particular reference to the
                    development of international air transport.</p>
                <p>The Department of State hopes that it will be possible in the first instance to
                    discuss these matters with the British and Canadian Governments and believes
                    that such discussions would be facilitated if an early indication could be
                    received of the views of the British Government on this general subject.</p>
                <pb facs="0376" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>
                <p>A similar communication is being addressed to the Canadian Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-26">January 26,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
